    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201843725058_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Online Learning and Distance Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title:  Executive Director of Online Learning and Distance Education Department:  Office of Online and Distance Education Reports To:  Associate Provost for Academic Excellence Appointment: Full-time; 40 hours per week (12-month position) Status: Exempt Bradley University seeks an accomplished, collaborative, and visionary leader to serve as Executive Director of Online Learning and Distance Education. Reporting to the Associate Provost for Academic Excellence, the candidate will provide strategic leadership for the University's online learning ecosystem, serving as the institutional champion for high-quality, student-centered online education.  The Executive Director will lead the development and execution of a university-wide vision for online learning that aligns with Bradley's mission, strategic priorities, and commitment to academic excellence. Working collaboratively with various university units, the Executive Director will cultivate a shared sense of purpose and collective momentum to expand Bradley's reach through innovative online learning opportunities. This is an on-campus position with oversight of a hybrid team. Key Responsibilities Build strong partnerships with deans, department chairs, faculty, and administrative leaders to create broad institutional ownership of online education initiatives.  Lead the strategic expansion of Bradley's portfolio of online and hybrid academic programs, certificates, and professional education offerings.  Guide market-informed program development by collaborating with academic units to identify opportunities aligned with workforce needs and student demand.  Champion excellence in online pedagogy, instructional design, accessibility, quality assurance, and student engagement.  Foster innovation through the thoughtful adoption of emerging educational technologies, including artificial intelligence and digital learning tools, while ensuring they support effective teaching and learning.  Collaborate with Enrollment Management, Marketing and Communications, and academic leadership to strengthen recruitment, retention, and student success for online learners.  Establish metrics and assessment practices to evaluate program quality, learner outcomes, operational effectiveness, and return on investment.  Oversee federal and state compliance for various programs. About the Office The Office of Online and Distance Education partners with faculty and academic units across the University to design, develop, and support high-quality online learning experiences. The office provides expertise in instructional design, educational technology, faculty development, quality standards, project management, and strategic program support while working collaboratively to advance Bradley University's educational mission. Bradley University offers a growing portfolio of undergraduate, graduate, doctoral, certificate, and professional education programs delivered in online and hybrid formats. As learner expectations and workforce needs continue to evolve, the University is committed to expanding flexible, accessible, and academically rigorous educational opportunities that serve traditional students, adult learners, and working professionals. Qualifications Preferred qualifications include: Master's degree required; earned doctorate or other terminal degree preferred.  Significant leadership experience in online learning, digital education, instructional design, academic innovation, or a related area within higher education.  Demonstrated success developing and implementing strategic initiatives that require collaboration across multiple academic and administrative units.  Experience leading organizational change and building consensus among diverse stakeholders.  Knowledge of current and emerging trends in online learning, digital pedagogy, instructional technologies, learning management systems (Canvas), artificial intelligence, accessibility, learning analytics, and student success. Experience supporting faculty in the design and delivery of high-quality online instruction.  Strong communication, project management, and organizational leadership skills.  Proven track record of managing remote or hybrid professionals (e.g., instructional designers, educational technologists, and adjunct staff). Ability to establish clear communication protocols, streamline asynchronous workflows, and foster a strong, collaborative team culture within a distributed work environment. Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for a minimum of three professional references with telephone numbers.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201852098656_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Annual Fund Gift Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Annual Fund Gift Officer Department: Advancement Reports To: Executive Director of Donor Engagement Appointment: Full-time, 40 hours per week (12-month position), On Campus Status: Exempt Position Summary The Annual Fund Gift Officer is a front-facing fundraiser responsible for building meaningful relationships with alumni, parents, friends, and Peoria-area community members whose annual giving is generally under $10,000. The officer will qualify, cultivate, solicit, renew, upgrade, and steward a portfolio of donors and prospective donors, with particular emphasis on expanding the Lydia Moss Bradley Society and increasing unrestricted support through the Bradley Fund. This role advances Bradley University’s goals to grow the number of donors, increase alumni participation, strengthen retention and renewal rates, encourage higher levels of annual support, and develop a well-qualified pipeline for major gift portfolios. The officer will engage donors directly through phone and email outreach, virtual and in-person meetings, campus and regional events, and other personalized strategies. The Annual Fund Gift Officer reports to the Executive Director of Donor Engagement and works collaboratively with the Senior Director of the Bradley Fund, the Assistant Director of Annual Giving, and the Assistant Director of Donor Relations. The manager also partners closely with the Vice President for Advancement, Major Gift Officers, Alumni Relations, Advancement Services, and campus colleagues to provide a coordinated, donor-centered experience. Key Responsibilities Portfolio Fundraising and Donor Engagement Build and manage a portfolio of annual giving donors and prospective donors, primarily at the $1,000 to $9,999 level, while cultivating selected donors below $1,000 who demonstrate strong affinity or potential for increased support. Develop and execute individualized strategies to identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit, renew, upgrade, and steward donors through phone calls, emails, virtual conversations, in-person meetings, events, and other personal outreach. Conduct meaningful donor contacts and visits and make direct gift solicitations in support of the Bradley Fund and other University priorities. Build relationships with Bradley alumni nationwide and Peoria-area community members, connecting their interests with opportunities to support students and the University. Secure annual commitments, recurring gifts, multi-year pledges when appropriate, and renewed or increased support in alignment with established goals. Lydia Moss Bradley Society Growth Make growth of the Lydia Moss Bradley Society a central focus by identifying, cultivating, and soliciting donors for fully unrestricted annual gifts of $1,000 or more to the Bradley Fund. Develop strategies to retain current Society members, renew lapsed members, upgrade donors into higher recognition levels, and welcome new members through personalized outreach and stewardship. Partner with the Senior Director of the Bradley Fund, Donor Relations, the Society’s volunteer leadership, and university leaders on membership communications, recognition, events, and other engagement opportunities. Annual Giving Initiatives and Collaboration Support the planning and execution of the Bradley Fund’s annual fundraising program, including Day of Giving, targeted appeals, digital campaigns, special initiatives, giving-society efforts, and fiscal year-end outreach. Coordinate closely with the Assistant Director of Annual Giving so that direct donor outreach complements broad-based mail, email, digital, text, and phone strategies. Collaborate with the Associate Director of Donor Relations to ensure assigned donors receive timely, accurate, and meaningful acknowledgment, recognition, impact reporting, and stewardship. Attend and support alumni, donor, campus, and community events, using these opportunities to deepen relationships, identify prospective donors, and advance follow-up strategies. Work with Alumni Relations and campus partners to convert engagement into philanthropy and connect annual giving with the broader Bradley experience. Pipeline Development and Advancement Partnership Identify annual donors with the interest, engagement, and potential to become major gift prospects, and collaborate with the Vice President for Advancement and Major Gift Officers on qualification and transition strategies. Participate in regular portfolio and pipeline reviews, sharing donor intelligence, progress, next steps, and recommended assignments or handoffs. Coordinate outreach with colleagues to avoid duplication, honor existing relationships, and deliver one consistent Bradley donor experience. Prepare donor briefings, contact summaries, solicitation plans, proposals, and follow-up materials as needed. Data Management and Performance Record substantive donor contacts, visits, solicitations, proposals, commitments, interests, and next steps promptly and accurately in Bradley’s CRM, Raiser’s Edge. Maintain accurate portfolio, pipeline, forecast, and pledge information and use data to prioritize outreach and evaluate results. Track and report progress toward annual goals for donor contacts, visits, solicitations, dollars raised, Lydia Moss Bradley Society membership, donor acquisition, retention, renewal, upgrades, and qualified major gift referrals. Use donor data, giving history, engagement information, and available prospect research to develop segmented and personalized outreach strategies. Performance Expectations Meet or exceed annual fundraising, activity, retention, upgrade, membership, and pipeline goals established with the Executive Director of Donor Engagement. Demonstrate disciplined portfolio management, consistent personal outreach, timely follow-through, and a strong commitment to donor service. Contribute to growth in total donors and alumni donors, Bradley Fund revenue, Lydia Moss Bradley Society membership, donor renewal rates, and the number of qualified prospects referred to Major Gift Officers. Maintain the highest standards of confidentiality, integrity, professionalism, collaboration, and donor-centered conduct. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. At least two years of successful fundraising, annual giving, relationship management, sales, business development, alumni engagement, customer development, or closely related experience. Demonstrated ability to build relationships, communicate persuasively, ask for financial commitments, and move donors or clients toward decisions. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and follow-through skills. Ability to manage a portfolio and multiple priorities independently while contributing effectively to a collaborative team. Comfort using data, goals, and performance measures to guide work and assess progress. Proficiency with Google Suite, Microsoft Office and willingness to use a constituent relationship management system consistently and accurately. Ability and willingness to travel regionally and occasionally beyond the region and attend evening and weekend meetings and events. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education advancement, annual giving, nonprofit development, membership development, or a similar relationship-driven environment. Experience managing a donor or client portfolio and successfully renewing or increasing financial commitments. Experience with Raiser’s Edge, GiveCampus, Almabase, or comparable fundraising and engagement platforms. Knowledge of Bradley University, its alumni community, or the Peoria region. Work Environment This position is based at Bradley University in Peoria, Illinois. The role requires regular interaction with donors and prospective donors and includes local, regional and national travel, campus and community events, and occasional evening and weekend responsibilities. Other duties may be assigned in support of Bradley University’s Advancement goals. Qualified candidates should submit a cover letter, resume and complete contact information for a minimum of three professional references with telephone numbers.  Please submit all materials at the time of initial application .  Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employment with Bradley University is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA, and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. Information regarding our benefits can be found here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/ Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5,000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=df6f93d4-2277-4999-ac63-88a55668ffd3&ccId=9200110706773_2&jobId=9201851352524_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Grounds Maintenance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nPosition Title: Grounds Maintenance Department:     Facilities Management Reports to:       Grounds Supervisor Appointment:   Full-time; 40 hours per week, 1st Shift (7:00 am - 3:30 pm) Status:             Non-Exempt Pay Rate:          $22.00 per hour (21.75 to start then $22 per hour after completion of the Teamster's 60-day probationary period). DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES   Provide grounds maintenance support to Facilities Management. Grounds Maintenance includes but is not limited to: preparation, planting, mowing repair, replacement and renovation of ground covers, plants, shrubs, sidewalks, streets and lots; small tree removal and pruning; operation and maintenance of surface and sewer water systems as well as manual and computer based irrigation systems; use, operate, and maintain tools and equipment including tractors, mowers, snowplows, and material handling; operate and use moderate to heavy equipment in efficient safe manner; refuse and garbage maintenance; move and haul property as instructed; some limited brick and concrete work and maintenance of retaining walls; carry out all duties in safe and efficient manner  consistent with University policies and procedures. Varying amount of after hour and special event hours as needed; perform other related duties as assigned.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS   Proven experience with and knowledge of grounds maintenance procedures as stated above; previous experience with manual and power operated equipment including all types of mowers, edgers, chainsaws, etc. related to this position; good comprehensive skills including ability to read and comprehend verbal and written instructions; prior experience operating all related implements and equipment with agility and safety; work as a team and independently; ability to operate forklift; demonstrated good safety, attendance and work record; must have a valid Illinois driver’s license; D.O.T. medium weight truck physical required. Selected candidate must become member of the Teamsters, Chauffeurs and Helpers Local Union.   MENTAL/PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Selected candidate must have the mental and physical capabilities to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation; ability to tolerate constant or extreme noise, independently handle minimum 50 pounds; visual ability to operate equipment effectively and safely; hearing ability to hold conversations through earpiece and in person; speaking ability to effectively communication with other individuals; work environment is primarily outdoor. Ability to tolerate extreme temperatures while working outside is also required. APPLICATION PROCEDURE Please complete the online application process and upload a resume, c omplete contact information for three professional references, and any certificates and/or licenses. Please submit all materials at the time of initial application.  Applications will begin being reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled.  Employment at Bradley University is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of a criminal background check, pre-employment physical, and drug screen.  Bradley University offers a competitive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life and disability coverages, FSA, HSA and retirement plan options. Bradley also offers significant higher education cost savings for employees and dependents through the Tuition Remission program. More information regarding our benefits is available here:  https://www.bradley.edu/offices/business/human-resources/benefits/  . Bradley University is a top-ranked, private university in Peoria, Illinois, offering nearly 5.000 undergraduate and graduate students’ opportunities, choices, and resources to build their futures. Innovation, action, and collaboration drive Bradley students to generate ideas and create solutions that remake the world around them. Our comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate academic programs includes business, communications, education, engineering, fine arts, health sciences, liberal arts and sciences, and technology. Bradley University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The administration, faculty and staff are committed to attracting qualified candidates from underrepresented groups.",
